ls; it exposes a sign-in reading; route and outcomes are left to IF-283 and IF-284 -> upward, it now traces to SR-227 (the coordinator route's retained launch, the sign-in reading) and to SR-231 (admission and current evidence), and its rationale says which clause serves which. Sideways, it composes LLR-305's request rather than restating it, and refers to the IF contracts by id. Downward, TC-321 verifies the entry clauses, and the sign-in command's printed reading is verified by TC-323's `test_the_signin_command_prints_the_probe_result` -> ready.\n- [APPROVE] TC-321 -> only a claimed lane launches, writing one attributed log per call; a second coordinator call resumes the first's session; a session at the dial drains and retires at the next clear point; the default route is ANTHROPIC-OPUS-STRONG; a newly reserved path is owned by its call alone, with missing parents created; a sign-in refusal releases the reservation and exits 7; IF-284 gives 0 only for this call's valid in-deadline verdict, 1 for a failed, timed-out, missing or invalid verdict, and 2 for each named pre-launch refusal -> Verifies now lists SR-227 beside SR-231, LLR-306 and IF-283..IF-285, matching what it asserts; the two coordinator-route lifecycle tests are back in Evidence and Method, and Expected states SR-227's \"second coordinator-route adjudication resumes\" clause and the clear-point drain; Expected and Method cover the same conditions -> ready.\n\nThe approval act flips these three rows and snapshots all three registries in\na separate commit.\n\nOUTCOME: APPROVE rows=3\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1968,"cache_read_input_tokens":178720,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1968},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_managemen